## github/codeql - derived review-check knowledge

**Files:** `src/MeisterDev.ProPR.ProRV/Assets/**` (embedded into the ProRV assembly)
**Upstream:** https://github.com/github/codeql
**Licence:** MIT - `Copyright (c) 2006-2025 GitHub, Inc.`

ProRV's check catalog is derived from the metadata of the CodeQL queries: each check keeps the identity of the
query it came from (the query's path, its `@kind`, `@precision`, `@severity` and CWE tags) and reproduces the
query's own one-line description. The review guidance wrapped around each check - what to look for, when a check
stops being relevant to a diff - is ProPR's own, and no CodeQL query code, QL library code, or CodeQL binary is
included or executed. What is redistributed is the derived metadata and those descriptions, which is why the
notice below travels with it.

